// Attempt 54 regressed by using invalid helpers (`CSDHelpers.PrefixToString`,
// `CSDHelpers.CountSubstring`) that aren't in the allowed method set.
//
// Strategy: keep attempt 43's proven span-management skeleton but replace the
// inner GroupBoostedConstrainedStep loop with a single call to
// RegenerateUnitOnGroundingFailure, which specifically detects ungrounded
// schema identifiers (table/column names not found in the prompt context),
// rolls back to the last accepted checkpoint, and resamples with a persistent
// penalty on the rejected identifier.  This directly targets the
// 141/300 syntax_valid_wrong failure cluster.
//
// Structure:
//   Phase 1: ≤5 unconstrained steps for "SQL: " preamble
//   Phase 2: Force "<<" open if not already entered
//   Phase 3: RegenerateUnitOnGroundingFailure(budget=840, retries=4, rollback=30)
//             to generate a schema-grounded SQL prefix
//   Phase 4: CloseConstrainedSpan if complete; else CloseSpanWithinBudget(80)
//
// Budget arithmetic (maxSteps=900): preamble ≤6, Phase 3 ≤840,
//   Phase 4 ≤54 → total ≤900 ✓
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// Invariant 1 (parser_validity):
//   insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
//
//   Phase 1 (unconstrained loop): insideConstrainedOut flips true only when
//     RenderedEndsWith(generated,"<<") is satisfied, at which point we set
//     currentConstrainedOut:=[] and IsValidPrefix([]) holds by precondition.
//     On EOS break insideConstrainedOut stays false; implication vacuous.
//
//   Phase 2 (OpenConstrainedSpan): only runs when !insideConstrainedOut; sets
//     currentConstrainedOut:=[], which is parser-valid by precondition.
//
//   Phase 3 (RegenerateUnitOnGroundingFailure): postcondition guarantees
//     parser.IsValidPrefix(resultConstrained); we assign
//     currentConstrainedOut:=resultConstrained while insideConstrainedOut
//     stays true; invariant preserved.
//
//   Phase 4a (CloseConstrainedSpan): sets insideConstrainedOut:=false; the
//     implication becomes vacuously true and currentConstrainedOut:=[].
//   Phase 4b (CloseSpanWithinBudget): its postcondition guarantees
//     insideOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentOut) directly.
//
// Invariant 2 (progress):
//   |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps
//
//   Phase 1: UnconstrainedStep increments steps by 1 and appends ≤1 token;
//     the 1:1 ratio preserves the invariant each iteration.
//
//   Phase 2: OpenConstrainedSpan appends exactly 1 "<<" token and increments
//     steps by 1; 1:1, invariant preserved.
//
//   Phase 3: RegenerateUnitOnGroundingFailure postcondition gives
//     |resultConstrained| <= |currentConstrainedOut_before| + grndBudget.
//     |stablePrefix| = |generated_before| - |currentConstrainedOut_before|.
//     So |generated_after| = |stablePrefix| + |resultConstrained|
//       <= |generated_before| + grndBudget
//       <= |generatedPrefix| + steps_before + grndBudget
//       = |generatedPrefix| + steps_after. ✓
//     steps grows by grndBudget = remaining - closeReserve, ensuring
//     steps_after = maxSteps - closeReserve < maxSteps.
//
//   Phase 4a: CloseConstrainedSpan appends ≤1 ">>" per +1 step; 1:1 ✓.
//   Phase 4b: CloseSpanWithinBudget postcondition gives
//     |generatedOut| <= |generated| + budget while steps += budget ✓.
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END

